# Implementation Plan: Manim-Style Animation Overhaul

To match the Manim aesthetic, we will refine the animation engine with "organic" easing, add creation-based drawing effects for geometric objects, and implement higher-fidelity equation morphing.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The primary change is switching the default animation easing to a **Quintic (Smooth)** function. This will make all movements feel less mechanical and more like a produced math video.

## Proposed Changes

### 🧪 Animation Engine Overhaul

#### [MODIFY] [animations.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/core/animations.ts)
- Add `smooth` easing: `t => t*t*t * (t * (t * 6 - 15) + 10)`.
- Update `animate` to use `smooth` as the default easing function.
- Add `lagRatio` support for sequence animations (Manim's `LaggedStart`).

### 🎨 Geometry Creation Effects

#### [MODIFY] [canvas-renderer.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/renderers/canvas-renderer.ts)
- Implement `ShowCreation` (aliased as `Create` in the spec).
- Update `drawVectorObj` and `drawLineObj` to support a `completion` property ($0 \to 1$).
- When `completion < 1`, the object will be drawn partially (e.g., as if it's being traced from origin to tip).

### 🖋️ Advanced Equation Morphing

#### [MODIFY] [equation-morph-renderer.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/renderers/equation-morph-renderer.ts)
- Implement "Smart Morphing": Automatically identify common terms between two LaTeX strings.
- Matching terms will animate their positions (`transform`), while new terms will `Write` or `FadeIn`.
- This replicates Manim's `ReplacementTransform` behavior for equations.

### ✨ Visual Polish

#### [MODIFY] [colors.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/utils/colors.ts)
- Update the palette with high-contrast Manim colors (Pure Teal, Deep Blue, Bright Gold).
- Darken the background to a deep slate (`#1b1b1b` equivalent) for more "premium" contrast.

#### [MODIFY] [style.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/style.css)
- Update typography for a more "mathematical paper" look (using Latin Modern or similar Serif subsets).

